READING RULE: a control is causally valid only if it passes all three:
  (A1) balance: |SMD| <= 0.10 (0.25 acceptable) on all 6 footprint covariates;
  (A2) neutrality: concept proxy shift <= 10% absolute and <= 15% of the concept edit's own shift;
  (A3) overlap: >= 95% of images can be calibrated to the exact strength of the concept edit.
  Test (T): neutral controls with different mechanisms must give equal CaCE (section C), and ĝ(M)
  must generalise to an unseen family (LOFO R2 > 0, section E). If (T) fails, the generic response
  is not a function of the measured footprint -> no control identifies ΔCaCE, and the bounds in
  section G are the real uncertainty of every 'placebo-corrected' score.
